    description: "MEASUREMENT ITEM, NOT A CODE ITEM. Do not write a fix against this until the question below is\nanswered. It is filed because it is the LARGEST MEASURED BLOCKER in the ADR-0017 section 3a area\nand no existing item covers it, while three filed items attack a conjunct four times smaller.\n\nWHAT WAS MEASURED (2026-08-05, dev c675fc484f). The section 3a walk only runs when guard2 passes:\n\n    if sink_call_lines and source_tracked and sink_after_source:\n\nAn instrument (meas/guard2_split.py) decomposed that conjunction by reading production own frame\nlocals. POSITIVE CONTROL: it reproduces the independently-measured site chain exactly - caddy\n169 -> 32 -> 16, pretix 873 -> 108 -> 35.\n\n  conjunct state at guard2               caddy /32   pretix /108   pooled /140\n  PASS (walk actually runs)                  16          35         51 (36.4%)\n  fails sink_after_source ALONE              12          42         54 (38.6%)\n  fails source_tracked + sink_after_source    3          19         22 (15.7%)\n  fails source_tracked ALONE                  1          12         13 ( 9.3%)\n\nsink_after_source is implicated in 76 of 140 pooled sites (54.3%) and is the SOLE blocker at 54\n(38.6%). By contrast source_tracked - the conjunct WI-losod-runaz attacks - is the sole blocker at\n13 (9.3%), and at just 1 of 32 caddy sites (3.1%).\n\nTHE HYPOTHESIS, AND IT IS NOT ESTABLISHED. meas/guard2_sizes.py shows 12 of caddy 15\nsink_after_source failures have exactly ONE recorded sink call line. The code own comment at\ntaint.py:2461-2467 describes a mechanism that would produce exactly that: ir.deduplicate_edges\nkeeps one edge per (src, dst, edge_type) carrying whichever call site was encountered FIRST, so a\nfunction calling fmt.Printf twelve times records one line. If the single recorded line is an\nARTIFACT of that dedup, then sink_after_source is comparing the source against an arbitrary one of\nN call sites and failing for a reason that has nothing to do with the code being analyzed.\n\nWHY IT IS NOT ESTABLISHED: I did not measure the TRUE call-site count per (function, callee), so I\ncannot distinguish \"one recorded line because dedup dropped eleven\" from \"one recorded line because\nthere genuinely is one call\". Those are different facts with identical surface, and only the first\nis a defect.\n\nPOSITIVE CONTROL ALREADY IN HAND: some sites DO carry 12 recorded sink lines, so meta.call_lines\nmultiplicity recovery demonstrably works and the mechanism is not globally inert. That makes the\nsingle-line cases interesting rather than expected.\n\nWHAT TO MEASURE, in order:\n  1. For each sink_after_source failure, the TRUE number of call sites of that callee inside that\n     caller, counted from the AST via production own parse - NOT from the edge, which is the thing\n     under suspicion.\n  2. Partition the 54 sole-blocker sites into (a) dedup dropped real later call sites that would\n     have passed sink_after_source, (b) genuinely one call site and the ordering verdict is\n     correct, (c) other.\n  3. Only if (a) is non-trivial, size a fix - and check its DIRECTION first. More passing walks\n     means more walks that can return False, and since PR #214 a False earns sanitized and a\n     sanitized flow is dropped from a claim violation set. A fix here can SUPPRESS findings. That\n     is the opposite direction from WI-votom and it must be argued explicitly, not assumed.\n\nDENOMINATOR CAVEATS: two repos (caddy go, pretix python) of a seven-repo pool; the other five\nproduce 0 walks each. Warm behavior-map cache. The 140 pooled sites are guard2 evaluations, not\ndistinct code locations.\n\nRELATED: WI-losod-runaz-korit-digos-lajos-vivuh-ronon-kukod attacks source_tracked and was ranked\nabove this on a population of AST CONSTRUCTS (700 of 6,596 go if-statements) rather than on blocked\nadjudications. Its measured ceiling on this cohort is <=4 additional adjudications out of 169 caddy\nsites, and 3 of those 4 would still be blocked by sink_after_source. Sequence accordingly."  # 437b
