  nonce: 1d05  # 1d05
  message: "ANSWERED, and the hypothesis is REFUTED. The single recorded sink call line is GROUND TRUTH, not a deduplicate_edges artifact. Full write-up + instruments: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/taint-area-08052026/WI-vimon-MEASUREMENT.md and meas/.\n\nMETHOD. meas/callsite_truth.py captures each guard2 site IDENTITY from productions own frame locals (the prior instrument recorded only the conjunct booleans, so there was nothing to look up a ground truth for). meas/ground_truth.py compares recorded sink call lines against the callee name occurrences in the callers source span. Positive control: reproduces guard2_split.py byte-identically on both repos, incl. the failset split (caddy 16/12/3/1, pretix 35/42/19/12). Denominator VERIFIED not assumed: apollo-server and zoxide show guard1_test=1 and never reach guard2, so caddy+pretix are the whole population.\n\nRESULT, recorded vs true call sites across all 76 sink_after_source failures:\n  caddy  15 failures: AGREES 15, RECORDED_FEWER 0, RECORDED_MORE 0\n  pretix 61 failures: AGREES 36, RECORDED_FEWER 25, RECORDED_MORE 0\n\ncaddy has ZERO under-counts. meta.call_lines multiplicity recovery works: printEnvironment records all twelve fmt.Printf lines [454-464,469]; cmdHashPassword records both sites of each of its two callees. Independently corroborated by reading caddys on-disk survey.json directly.\n\nTHE DECIDING NUMBER. A missing sink site only matters if it lands AFTER the source. Of the 25 RECORDED_FEWER, 24 have every missing site still PRECEDING the source; exactly 1 would flip sink_after_source. That is 1 of 76 pooled failures (1.3%), and 1 is an UPPER BOUND because the textual matcher over-matches and a spurious hit can only ADD a flip.\n\nCAUSE IS NOT DEDUP. All 25 under-counts trace to the PYTHON ANALYZER emitting ZERO call edges when the receiver is an attribute chain with a non-module root: Item.objects.create(...) emits, o2.payments.create(...) does not. Verified by direct repro (meas/py_zero_edge_check.py), positive-controlled on os.getenv (2 sites -> 2 edges). Filed separately.\n\nWARM-CACHE CAVEAT RETIRED: the cache paths fourth segment is a content hash over installed hypergumbo_* .py files, so a pre-call_lines map cannot be served. pretix was rebuilt COLD this run regardless.\n\nDIRECTION, as the item demanded. Suppression needs BOTH adjudicated True AND a same-function sanitizer (taint.py:2569-2575), and adjudicated = (walk is True) collapses False and None (taint.py:2529-2533), so a failing first walk leaves the flow SURVIVING at approximate. Passing guard2 is a precondition for suppression, not suppression itself. Net direction of an emission fix is NOT determined here: more sink edges is also more sink SITES, which is expansive.\n\nTWO CORRECTIONS TO THIS ITEMS OWN NUMBERS. (1) The chain 169->32->16 is guard1_test -> guard2_test -> PASS-count, NOT guard1_passed (64/216). (2) s3a_walk_invoked over-counts exactly 3x (caddy 48=3x16, pretix 105=3x35) because its anchor is the first line of a five-line call expression; guard2_split.py and guard2_sizes.py carry the same artifact. The accurate counter already present is barrier_guard_test."  # 1d05
